  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two cells are connected in opposition as shown. Cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> emf and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> internal resistance; the cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> emf and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> internal resistance. The terminal potential difference of cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0056_93f3b89d262f.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 138px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0056_467c4927e5a8.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 122px;\"/></p><p>Current in circuit, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Applying Kirchhoff's law from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  }
